M_ENROLLED_STUDENTS>=1 GROUP BY DEPARTMENT_NAME` with `AVG`/`STDDEV`.\n- **dw_3985 (DeptCounts)**: precedent for \"departments that offer more than N subjects in that term\" → `COUNT(*) FROM COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED WHERE EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE = <term> GROUP BY DEPARTMENT_NAME HAVING COUNT(*) > 5`.\n- **dw_3131 / dw_2737**: classification template for \"at least 20% greater/less\" → `CASE WHEN x > avg*1.2 THEN 'HIGH_...' WHEN x < avg*0.8 THEN 'LOW_...' ELSE 'AVERAGE...' END` (both precedents use strict `>`/`<` with 1.2/0.8 multipliers).\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\nGraph traversal on ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER confirms: joins to ACADEMIC_TERMS (TERM_CODE) and ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL; membership in `concept_academic_term_dimension` and `column_concept_term_code`. Hint join keys confirm: ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE ↔ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE; SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE ↔ SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.OFFER_DEPT_CODE. Notably, **no term join key is given for SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY** — matching dw_3644 where the dept stats subquery is not term-restricted.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences & Task Fitness\n\n3a/3b. **Term-restricted subject population**: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (via EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE, term-linked, has DEPARTMENT_NAME, no enrollment) vs SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (has TOTAL_UNITS + NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, but no term join key provided in hints). The measure columns (TOTAL_UNITS, NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS filters) exist ONLY in SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY → stats must come from there. The \"in those terms\" count must come from the term-linked table (COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED), per dw_3985 precedent.\n\n3c. **Wording anchoring**: \"term indicator is 'C'\" → ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.TERM_INDICATOR; \"academic year\" → ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR; \"department name of the offered subject\" → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME; \"running sum of academic years within each department\" → window SUM over PARTITION BY DEPARTMENT_NAME (dw_3294/dw_4019 exact pattern); \"at least 3 subjects in those terms\" → COUNT(*) ≥ 3 on the 'C'-term catalog rows (dw_3985 pattern); \"more than 0 total units and at least 1 enrolled student\" → TOTAL_UNITS > 0 AND NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS >= 1 (dw_3644 exact pattern).\n\n3d. **Precedent counts**: running-sum-with-term-indicator-'C' precedents: 2 (dw_3294, dw_4019); dept avg/STDDEV with same filter wording: 1 (dw_3644); dept subject-count-in-term HAVING: 1 (dw_3985); 20%-classification CASE: 2 (dw_3131, dw_2737).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\nACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER resolves relative term references; COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED serves catalog-attribute questions per term; SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY serves enrollment/unit statistics per department; SIS_DEPARTMENT bridges department codes to names.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\nAll Phase 1 entities investigated: 5 gold tables (semantic_get ✓), precedents dw_3294/dw_4019/dw_3644/dw_3985/dw_3131/dw_2737/dw_1393/dw_2335/dw_4405/dw_3311/dw_2957 (semantic_get ✓), concepts concept_academic_term_dimension / concept_subject_offering_facts / concept_department_dimension (search desc ✓), column concepts term_code / year_columns / total_units / enrollment_measures / department_name (search desc ✓), graph traversal on ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER ✓. mysql_query attempted 7 times — all failed with server-side auth error `1045 Access denied for 'root'@'localhost'`, so runtime verification is impossible; the SQL is built strictly from documented columns and precedent SQL templates.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n6a/6b. Use the dw_3294 TermParams CTE (term parameter 'C' → terms → catalog subjects, with the running-sum window), filter departments via dw_3985-style HAVING COUNT(*) >= 3 on those term rows, attach dw_3644-style DeptStats (SIS_DEPARTMENT ⋈ SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, TOTAL_UNITS>0, NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS>=1, AVG/STDDEV per department name), and classify with the dw_3131 CASE template (>avg*1.2 / <avg*0.8). Inner joins guarantee every row has stats and a valid classification. No rounding.\n\n6c. **Data**: measure/filter columns exist only in SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY; term linkage only via EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE. **Semantic-network**: hint join keys exactly match the chosen join paths; precedent SQLs retrieved verbatim. **Business**: identical question-wording fragments map 1:1 to precedent metrics.\n\n6d. Tie-breaker note: \"at least 20%\" precedents (dw_3131, dw_2737) consistently implement it as strict `>` / `<` against the 1.2/0.8 multipliers — I follow that template.\n\n",
